<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Storm Gate</h1>
<p>Sphere: Mind Sphere
Class: none (no guild teaches it)
Mana: 15
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast storm gate &lt;gate&gt;
enter gate
</pre>
<p>The caster raises a clenched fist, mumbles 'Oofquah' and calls on the 
forces of nature to open a storm gate: a swirling storm cloud that drifts 
about the world, never long in one place. Cast on a gate, the spell opens 
it with a whoosh, and it stays open for a while, longer the greater your 
brain; then it closes with a hiss. Cast on anything else, you only pretend 
that it is a storm gate.
</p><p>While the gate is open, enter it to be carried away to the Ivory Path. The 
passage is rough: a weak body and mind may collapse on the way, and a 
clumsy step can fling you somewhere else entirely. A closed gate won't let 
you in, nor will it take you while you are fighting; and a storm gate that 
is attacked explodes.
</p><p>No guild teaches it, but it turns up on wands and scrolls among random 
treasure.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mind Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>